# LF everywhere, checked out as LF even on Windows.
#
# `upstream.sha256` is fed to sha256sum, which reads a trailing CR as part of
# the filename and reports every line as "no such file" — a checksum failure
# that looks exactly like Espressif having edited the file. The C also travels
# into a QEMU tree that is LF throughout.
#
# Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, so without this the
# portability build fails on the one check whose whole job is to be trusted.
* text eol=lf
